{
  "title": "Calorie estimates poll every 2 s with no end, and iOS drops a good estimate on one failed poll",
  "description": "Both clients POST /api/recipes/estimate-calories every 2 s while the response says `resolving` (ramekin-ios/Ramekin/CalorieEstimateSection.swift, ramekin-ui/src/components/CalorieEstimate.tsx). \
If the background resolver stalls (provider outage, worker backoff of up to an hour), that never stops. \
Reads no longer queue names, but they still queue weight gaps until p2-calorie-weights-in-catalog lands (server/src/api/recipes/estimate_calories.rs). \
On iOS, one failed poll after a good result clears the estimate. \
Fix on both clients: back off (for example 2 s doubling to 30 s) and stop after a few minutes, keeping the last good estimate on error. \
Mirror the behavior and tests on web and iOS.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
